+# frames from the encoder's own running clock whenever that is within 500 ms
+# of the commit's timestamp, so the same startup rebases leave frames stamped
+# early (frames sent at 72.7 ms of lead while the commit timeline sat at 82).
+# The clock exists for encoders that hold audio back; ours encodes each 10 ms
+# chunk into exactly 10 ms of frames, so when the frames cover exactly the
+# input the commit's timestamp is the right one. Anything else is left to the
+# library. Replaces push_stream._encode_for_transform_key (aiosendspin 9.1.1).
+_ps_encode = _ps._encode_for_transform_key
